y not be empty.Waiting after staging...Waiting for SOI change to Waiting for liftoff...Waiting for orbit...Waiting for transfer window to {0}... {1:F0}minWaiting for window to Walk (Arcade)Walk (FPS)Walking assembly: WaltWarningWarning Warning, MapObject Warning: Warning: PatchRendering Trajectory is NullWarning: Tried to search for a part with ID 0Warp HelperWarp HereWarp Rate limits for Warp to apoapsisWarp to periapsisWarping down...  UT: Warping to UT:Warping to apoapsis...Warping to apoapsis... {0:F0}s remainingWarping to periapsis...Warping to periapsis... {0:F0}s remainingWarping...WaterWaterFXWayPointMinDistanceWayPointMultiplierWayPointTriggerRangeWaypointWaypoint "{0}"Waypoint HelpWaypoint IndexWaypoint RadiusWaypointDefaultRewardWaypointsWeWebClient does not support concurrent I/O operations.WedWednesdayWeekWeightWeight DataWeightAcceptDeltaWeightDeclineDeltaWeightDefaultWeightMaximumWeightMinimumWeightWithdrawReadDeltaWeightWithdrawSeenDeltaWeld Heading AcquiredWeld Part CompleteWeld StartedWeld Turn to face PartWeldLock_Welding partWell done! You are in a great position to just lower your orbit and start descending on duna.

 When landing remember to deploy your ship's legs by right clicking them and clicking the button and aerobraking burning retrograde to reduce your speed. In a planet such as Duna a parachute helps somewhat, but it won't be enough to break your fall.

 All the very same principles you used here apply to traveling to any other planet or Celestial Body in General, so you are definitely ready to go on and conquer space. 

I'm really proud of you, I know you have potential.Welsh (United Kingdom)WernherWhack A KerbalWhack-A-KerbalWhat base portion of the total World First contract reward is granted passivelyWhat contracts call Molniya orbitsWhat contracts call geostationary orbits of the home planetWhat contracts call geosynchronous orbits of the home planetWhat contracts call heliostationary orbits of the SunWhat contracts call heliosynchronous orbits of the SunWhat contracts call stationary orbits of any other planetWhat contracts call synchronous orbits of any other planetWhat to multiply rewards by on hard requests like returning from atmospheric landingsWheelWheel Brakes torqueWheel DamageWheel LoadWheel Motor torqueWheel RetractedWheelColliderWheelCollidersWheelCollidersIgnoreWheelRBConstraintsWheelStateWheel_Piston_ColliderWheelsWheelspinWhen called from '{0}', rewriting a node of type '{1}' must return a non-null value of the same type. Alternatively, override '{2}' and change it to not visit children of this type.When revert is disabledWhen revert is enabledWhen setting up a transfer orbit using the Oberth effect you usually have to be very patient, it's all about being in the right place at the right time, sometimes it can take weeks, months or even years.

If you look at your mission timer you can see we spawned you close to the transfer window. Outside of training I recommend you speed up time in the Tracking Station if you don't want to wait that long. But how do you know exactly how long you have to wait? Well, that's complicated. The simplest way to guide you is with something called phase angles between the Kerbin and the CB you want to go to taking the Sun as reference. The phase angle to use on Duna is about 45 degrees. Calculating phase angles is beyond the scope of this tutorial, they're not too hard to find pre-calculated in "external resources".When skin temp / max skin temp greater than this, edge highlighting becomes visibleWhen skin temp / max skin temp greater than this, gauges become visibleWhen supplying a FieldInfo for fixing up a nested type, a valid ID for that containing object must also be supplied.When supplying the ID of a containing object, the FieldInfo that identifies the current field within that object must also be supplied.Where failed.Whether World First ignores first launch, reach space, and orbit homeWhether World First ignores the line of contracts after the tutorialWhether or not this docking port is attached to another docking port.Whether survey can spawn at high altitudes including orbitWhether survey can spawn at low altitudesWhether survey can spawn in the oceanWhether survey can spawn in vacuumWhether survey can spawn on the groundWhether survey requires an EVAWhether survey requires crew presenceWhether to allow Molniya orbits at allWhether to allow asteroid embedded station requests at allWhether to allow compound recoveries of kerbals and parts at allWhether to allow equatorial orbits at allWhether to allow kerbal only rescues at allWhether to allow landed recoveries on atmospheric planets at allWhether to allow landed recoveries on vacuum planets at allWhether to allow landing requests on the home planet at allWhether to allow mobile outpost requests at allWhether to allow 