The RUN ONCE or RUNONCEPATH concept
does not work from the interpreter
because the interpreter always
recompiles and re-runs the program
each run anyway.  'ONCE' only has meaning
when a program runs another program.
&
Because PRESERVE alters the behavior of the
trigger body it's inside of, it doesn't mean
anything when it's not inside a trigger like
WHEN or ON.
€ð
Because RETURN causes the current user function to quit
it doesn't mean anything when it's not inside a
user function.
